<section class="section section--tint">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>The details that decide whether a card is right</h2>
    <p class="lede" style="margin-top:12px;max-width:64ch">
      Any software can average some numbers. These are the cases that produce a
      card a parent can argue with.
    </p>
    <div class="grid grid--2" style="margin-top:34px">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>A paper not sat is not a zero</h3>
        <p>
          A pupil who was absent for one paper and a pupil whose marks have not
          been entered yet are different situations, and treating either as zero
          produces a card that is wrong. Both are tracked as what they are, and a
          card with a paper still outstanding says PROVISIONAL on it.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Practicals kept apart from theory</h3>
        <p>
          A practical is marked out of its own maximum, shown separately on the
          card, and combined with the theory for the pass mark. A subject that
          has no practical component cannot be given practical marks at all, so
          the two columns cannot quietly disagree.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Streams: nobody is marked out of the wrong syllabus</h3>
        <p>
          Where a class splits into streams, an Arts pupil is not marked against
          the Science papers and vice versa. The denominator for each pupil is
          the papers that pupil was actually meant to sit.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Your grading scale, and term weightage</h3>
        <p>
          Bands and grade points are yours to set, including a 10 point GPA if
          that is what your board uses. Term weightage is a setting too: if the
          final carries 70 per cent, the session mark carries the other 30 and
          the card says so.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="note" style="margin-top:26px">
      <p>
        Not built, and worth saying: <b>credit weighted GPA</b>. Every paper counts
        as one credit. A school running unequal credit hours gets an unweighted
        mean, which for almost every Pakistani school is the same number.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>Results are released when you say so</h2>
    <p class="lede" style="margin-top:12px;max-width:64ch">
      Marks being entered is not the same as results being published. A card is
      not visible to a parent until it is released, so a teacher can enter marks
      on Tuesday and the school can hold them until Friday.
    </p>
    <p style="margin-top:16px;max-width:66ch">
      A result can also be withheld for one pupil, which every school
      occasionally needs and few systems allow without deleting something. And a
      correction after release is a new version with the change recorded, not a
      quiet edit: one message per child per term, so a fix does not spam
      forty parents.
    </p>
    <p style="margin-top:20px">
      <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/parent-portal">How parents see a result</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

